      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T13:51:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I generally agree with Greg\u0027s sentiment, that this specific approach doesn\u0027t feel like quite the right way to get the BindGroups globally shared. DawnSharedContext does have the NoopFragmentShader module, which feels similar to this case, but I would prefer that we also remove it from the SharedContext when we have a good design.\n\nSharedContext was not really meant to be owning anything other than the base GPU access and then delegates to the other component types like QueueManager and GlobalCache. GlobalCache is where I\u0027d like to see these sorts of backend-specific shareable objects land. Besides pipelines, the GlobalCache manages owning the static vertex buffers that get created on initialization, so there\u0027s precedent for creating something once and then storing in the cache.\n\nThe main issue I think is that right now there\u0027s no backend-specific subclass of GlobalCache to add direct getters for these types of static backend resources. If getting these resources is a frequent operation, then it would make sense to have a DawnGlobalCache that holds these fields. On the other hand, currently these seem to be mostly used during pipeline creation, which should be infrequent, and while we want it to be fast, we could probably have an API on GlobalCache where you store a static resource associated with a ResourceKey.  Then during the Dawn backend initialization, it creates these bind group layouts and noop shader modules with resource keys.",
      "parentUuid": "90ce4399_4a42bb91",
      "revId": "5967d9d7f706a44ddd58f5a6faca66c927c9e5f0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
